course: dictionary
lesson: 8390
title: Everyday words: rucksack
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are used differently in different places. You may know a word, but people in another country might use a different one for the same thing. «Matthew put it back with one of his own, and walked home feeling light, as if he had put down a rucksack full of stones.» The clue is «feeling light»: he felt light because he had put something heavy down, so a rucksack is something heavy you carry.
explain: A rucksack is a bag you carry on your back, with two straps over your shoulders. In Britain, Ireland and parts of Australia, people say rucksack. In America, people usually say backpack, but both words are common everywhere, so you will understand either one.
explain: Packing a rucksack safely matters. Before a hike, pack water, snacks, a map, a coat and a first-aid kit. Always wear both straps, so the weight is spread evenly and your back is protected.
fact: A rucksack is a bag you carry on your back.
fact: A rucksack has two straps that go over your shoulders.
fact: Rucksack is the usual word in Britain, Ireland and parts of Australia.
fact: Americans usually say backpack, which means the same thing.
fact: For a hike, pack water, snacks, a map, a coat and a first-aid kit.
exercise: Matthew walked home feeling light, as if he had put down a rucksack full of stones. What is a rucksack? | A type of stone | *A bag you carry on your back | A small boat for the river | A kind of hat
exercise: Before a hike, what should you pack in your rucksack? | A television remote | Only a football and a comb | Nothing, because hikes are short | *Water, snacks, a map and a first-aid kit
exercise: Which word do Americans usually use for a rucksack? | *Backpack | Trolley | Handbag | Suitcase
test: Why should you wear both straps on your rucksack? | *To spread the weight evenly and protect your back | To stop it getting wet | To keep it closed | To make it look smart
test: In which places is rucksack the usual word? | America only | Everywhere in the world, with no differences at all | *Britain, Ireland and parts of Australia | Only on the moon
exam: Matthew feels light after putting down his rucksack. What does rucksack most likely mean? | A large wooden table | A type of road | A kind of dog | *A bag you carry on your back
